The construction is now pinned down: a binary Hamming code supplies the native \(e=1\) code, every received word is exactly \(t=e+\ell\) substitutions from the sampled codeword, and weight-\(t\) error masks are assembled in XOR-zero quadruples plus one three-mask identity whose XOR is a singleton. This keeps every channel marginally comparable, makes Theorem 28’s majority certificate executable, and creates a separate compact route (global XOR plus a Hamming syndrome) for Track B.
