codex
Implemented a complete Track B generator based on the paper’s native Hamming-space reconstruction problem. The paper’s Section 6 majority decoder is disclosed rather than hidden as a hardness claim. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2211.08812)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each; additionally 0/100 on an extended audit.
- Reference majority decoder: 8/8, 10,990 operations.
- Compact XOR/syndrome route: 8/8, 68 operations.
- Demo has exactly one valid answer among 2,048 codewords.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/gen_2211_08812.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only incomplete requirement is external oracle hardening: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded” for all three arms before any valid model attempt. Those errors are preserved and correctly recorded as 0/0 attempts—not model failures. No hardened verdict or rejection was fabricated.

After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2211_08812.py
```
