codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s native Hamming-space reconstruction problem. Section 6 explicitly supplies the \(\Theta(Nn)\) majority algorithm, while the constructed instances admit a shorter XOR-and-syndrome invariant route. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2211.08812v1)

Deliverables:

- [gen_2211_08812.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/gen_2211_08812.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2211.08812/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Exact shipping density: one valid codeword among \(2^{247}\).
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference majority decoder: 8/8, 10,990 counted operations.
- Compact route: 68 operations.
- Answer: 66 serialized characters, 255 bit-atoms.
- `escalate()` now correctly terminates with `cap_bound`.

The required external hardening remains incomplete: all bare, hinted, and placebo calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded,” yielding zero valid oracle attempts. The transcripts preserve those errors but do not establish hardness, so this result is not ready for submission until the OpenRouter quota is restored and the three harness runs are repeated.

Temporary G9 scratch directories were moved to trash after their transcripts were copied; they are recoverable.
