300:By Theorem \ref{RemarkNonConstantList}, we have $N\geq V(n,\ell-1)+1$.  Since $C$ is an $e$-error-correcting code and by Lemma \ref{Listasanat lahella POL}, we have $d(\bc_i,\bc_j)\in\{2e+1,2e+2\}$ for each $i\neq j$. Since we are considering binary Hamming space and $h\geq 3$, all pairwise distances cannot be $2e+1$. Let us assume without loss of generality that $d(\bc_1,\bc_2)=2e+2$ and let us then translate the Hamming space so that $\bc_1=\nolla$. Now $w(\bc_2)=2e+2$ and $w(\bc_3)\in\{2e+1,2e+2\}$. Moreover, $|\supp(\bc_2)\cap\supp(\bc_3)|=e+1$. Let $\overline{D}$ be any subset of $[1,n]$ satisfying $\supp(\bc_1+\bc_2) \cup \supp(\bc_1+\bc_3) \cup \supp(\bc_2+\bc_3) \subseteq \overline{D}$ and $|\overline{D}|=b$. Observe that $\supp(\bc_1)\setminus \overline{D}=\supp(\bc_2)\setminus \overline{D}=\supp(\bc_3)\setminus \overline{D}=\emptyset$.
