The partial oracle reply exposed a real flaw that the old adversary panel missed: at medium, Gemini recovered the answer by taking a hexadecimal-digit plurality, and a direct audit shows that heuristic solves 100/100 hard instances. That violates Track B’s required in-context failing attack, so the current module cannot ship despite its earlier self-test. I’m hardening the construction by making every bit nearly balanced across channels while preserving the exact XOR certificate and strict bitwise majority; this directly removes the visible “most rows share the same hex digit” signature.
