codex
The first `hard` oracle also solved the systematic-prefix version. That exposes a real design flaw: once the code says “the answer is this prefix,” majority need only scan those fixed 95 positions, so enlarging the ambient word does not enlarge the relevant haystack. I’m stopping this obsolete run and replacing that representation with a repetition-code construction whose short route is an intra-word block-XOR invariant; the strongest majority route must then process over ten thousand relevant bits while the exact shortcut stays under 300 digit operations.
