The replacement now survives a 200-seed attack sweep at every non-demo rung. At shipping, the paper’s full majority scan is 93,888 bits, the strongest construction-aware majority shortcut still needs 10,432 bit observations, and the intended block-XOR route is 128 explicit hex-digit operations. All six cheap/in-context attacks are 0/200, and the 64-bit witness remains fixed when channels double. I’m starting a fresh script-owned oracle run on this version.
